.TH ARIF_PINYIN 3 "Nov 03, 2026" 0.5.0 "ARIF User Manual"
.
.SH NAME
arif_pinyin - libpinyin integration for ARIF
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
.B #include <arif_pinyin.h>
.PP
.BI "extern struct arif_engine const " arif_pinyin_engine ;
.EE
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
Example implementation of an ARIF engine, powered by libpinyin.
.PP
See the manual page of
.BR arif_set_engine (3)
for how to use this engine.
.SS Initialization
The
.IR init ()
function of
.I arif_pinyin_engine
ignores the first argument.
Engine configuration is instead read from environment variables.
.PP
Note that the variables are only read during the first
.IR init ()
call, initialization of subsequent engine instances share the same
configuration.
.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ARIF_PINYIN_USER_DATA_DIR
Path to the libpinyin user data directory.
.IP
You may specify an empty directory, and libpinyin will initialize it for you.
Error message like "open user.conf failed" can be ignored.
.TP
.B ARIF_PINYIN_SYSTEM_DATA_DIR
Path to the libpinyin system-wide data directory.
.IP
Defaults to "/usr/lib/libpinyin/data".
.TP
.B ARIF_PINYIN_INPUT_MODE
Input mode for libpinyin.
Should be one of "full_pinyin", "double_pinyin" or "chewing" (case sensitive).
.IP
Defaults to "full_pinyin".
.TP
.B ARIF_PINYIN_INPUT_SCHEME
Input scheme for the specified input mode of libpinyin.
Value should be a decimal integer.
.IP
See libpinyin's "pinyin_custom2.h" header file for available input schemes
and default values.
.TP
.B ARIF_PINYIN_ADDON_LIBS
Addon phrase libraries of libpinyin to be loaded.
Value should be a comma-separated list of decimal integers.
.IP
See file "table.conf" under libpinyin's data directory for indices of
available addon phrase libraries.
.
